{"story":{"id":"7cc03b17-7698-4d8c-bd11-29d4d6881123","title":"The Lantern Keeper","description":"A keeper tends the last lantern on a drowned coast.","genre":"Fantasy","createdAt":"2026-09-30T00:29:33.840Z","updatedAt":"2026-09-30T00:31:57.775Z","wordCount":249,"entries":[{"id":"8493d357-95f5-4008-82e2-c3a5baf8574f","position":0,"source":"user","text":"You climb the tower stairs with the oil can.","actionKind":"do","inputText":"I climb the tower stairs with the oil can","variantGroupId":"8493d357-95f5-4008-82e2-c3a5baf8574f","variantIndex":0,"variantCount":1,"variantProfilesMixed":false,"generation":null,"costUsd":null,"reasoningTokens":null,"callStatus":null,"createdAt":"2026-09-30T00:31:49.076Z"},{"id":"4daeb9df-36ae-4be7-a1da-8ba92009ba4e","position":1,"source":"generated","text":"The light came in low and yellow across the floorboards, marking out the shapes of things that had been left where they fell. Dust turned slowly through it, patient as ash. Somewhere a clock kept time for no one in particular, and the sound of it was less a measure than a companion.\n\nFootsteps crossed the room above, paused, and went on. There was no need to look up; the ceiling told the whole story in its small complaints. A breath was drawn and held a beat too long before it was let go. Whatever had been decided in the hours before dawn had not yet been spoken aloud, and until it was, the morning could be pretended into something ordinary.","actionKind":null,"inputText":null,"variantGroupId":"4daeb9df-36ae-4be7-a1da-8ba92009ba4e","variantIndex":0,"variantCount":1,"variantProfilesMixed":false,"generation":{"modelId":"~anthropic/claude-sonnet-latest","thinking":"off","temperature":0.9,"profileName":"Default","promptTokens":417,"completionTokens":163},"costUsd":null,"reasoningTokens":null,"callStatus":null,"createdAt":"2026-09-30T00:31:50.620Z"},{"id":"9f0fb947-2e63-470f-a624-1801e6395f47","position":2,"source":"generated","text":"Wind came up off the water and turned the leaves over, showing their pale undersides the way they do before weather. The air smelled of iron and cut grass. Everything in that half-lit hour seemed to lean slightly toward what came next, as though the world were a sentence with its ending withheld.\n\nThe path narrowed where the hedges had grown untended, and the walking slowed to accommodate it. There was a gate at the end, and beyond the gate a field, and beyond the field the low grey shoulder of the hills. None of it had changed. That was the strange part — that so much could happen and the land would simply go on holding its shape.","actionKind":null,"inputText":null,"variantGroupId":"9f0fb947-2e63-470f-a624-1801e6395f47","variantIndex":0,"variantCount":1,"variantProfilesMixed":false,"generation":{"modelId":"~anthropic/claude-sonnet-latest","thinking":"off","temperature":0.9,"profileName":"Default","promptTokens":580,"completionTokens":160},"costUsd":null,"reasoningTokens":null,"callStatus":null,"createdAt":"2026-09-30T00:31:57.775Z"}],"entriesBefore":0,"charsBefore":0,"hasMoreBefore":false,"windowStartPosition":0,"generatedSpan":{"firstIso":"2026-09-30T00:31:50.620Z","lastIso":"2026-09-30T00:31:57.775Z"},"images":[{"id":"89198a41-8280-4cda-97fd-a271aca353dd","position":3,"imageGroupId":"89198a41-8280-4cda-97fd-a271aca353dd","imageIndex":0,"imageCount":1,"takes":[{"id":"89198a41-8280-4cda-97fd-a271aca353dd","prompt":"A keeper climbing a spiral lighthouse stair. Style: oil painting, visible brushwork, warm varnish.","aspectRatio":"16:9","mediaType":"image/svg+xml","modelId":"black-forest-labs/flux-1.1-pro","seed":1874440028,"createdAt":"2026-09-30T00:31:59.775Z"}],"prompt":"A keeper climbing a spiral lighthouse stair. Style: oil painting, visible brushwork, warm varnish.","sourcePrompt":"Wren on the stairs","promptLoreIds":[],"modelId":"black-forest-labs/flux-1.1-pro","aspectRatio":"16:9","seed":1874440028,"mediaType":"image/svg+xml","costUsd":null,"callStatus":null,"slotCostUsd":null,"slotUnpricedCalls":0,"createdAt"